{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03QD", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:80dcfef31e1e027cf57ab35b08d4d96c0958b5297715c4c642d168c727084561", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe begin by stating a theorem which has already been used many times\nin the Stacks project. There are many versions of this result; here we\njust state the algebraic version.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5ca5cbe9cd8758df9f7cdef36e4bdcc6a34a4e4a772115b2d986d1bf2c515bf0", "unit_id": "tag:03QD:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "theorem", "parent_tag": "03QD", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$A\\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathfrak p \\subset A$", "MATH_0003": "$A \\to A'$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathfrak p' \\subset A'$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathfrak p$", "MATH_0006": "$\\kappa(\\mathfrak p) = \\kappa(\\mathfrak p')$", "MATH_0007": "$ B \\otimes_A A' = B_1\\times \\ldots \\times B_r \\times C$", "MATH_0008": "$ A'\\to B_i$", "MATH_0009": "$q_i\\subset B_i$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathfrak p'$", "MATH_0011": "$\\Spec(C \\otimes_{A'} \\kappa(\\mathfrak p'))$", "MATH_0012": "$C$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathfrak p'$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{theorem}\n\\label{theorem-quasi-finite-etale-locally}\n", "suffix": "\\end{theorem}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ce95e45f9c8d859a99fc72582b7bea7bb5b29a4dfa93eba5e5fb8def1e43ff38", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:456f5b4ac0b3750b322141f741f2a82d6f9b417648b44c7f44971672361a449d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be finite type ring map and <MATH_0002> a prime\nideal. Then there exist an <ACCENT_0001>tale ring map <MATH_0003> and a prime\n<MATH_0004> lying over <MATH_0005> such that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<MATH_0006>,\n<STRUCT_0003>\n<MATH_0007>,\n<STRUCT_0004>\n<MATH_0008> is finite and there exists a unique prime <MATH_0009> lying\nover <MATH_0010>, and\n<STRUCT_0005> all irreducible components of the fibre\n<MATH_0011> of <MATH_0012> over <MATH_0013>\nhave dimension at least 1.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7f315649f6b6db4af74b8a0857f29593da56fcfabb414ec3c228540480ae07da", "unit_id": "tag:03QE:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03QD", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-etale-makes-quasi-finite-finite}", "REF_0002": "\\cite[Th\\'eor\\`eme 18.12.1]{EGA4}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{more-morphisms-section-etale-localization}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:23c9384b90e7d86421088b53840ec06823cbe38985404b579bd63d7f1c35722b", "source_text": "See Algebra, Lemma <REF_0001>, or\nsee <REF_0002>. For a slew of versions in terms of\nmorphisms of schemes, see\nMore on Morphisms, Section <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b0fcd70a61f5db9057f0cda72279e3516a961c205321ee171b87251f0b7bfbc5", "unit_id": "tag:03QE:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03QD", "placeholders": {"COMMENT_0001": "%10.01.09\n", "ITEMCLOSE_0001": "]", "ITEMCLOSE_0002": "]", "ITEMOPEN_0001": "\\item[", "ITEMOPEN_0002": "\\item[", "MATH_0001": "$f\\in \\mathbf{Z}_p[T]$", "MATH_0002": "$f \\bmod p = g_0 h_0$", "MATH_0003": "$gcd(g_0, h_0) = 1$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$f = gh$", "MATH_0006": "$\\bar g = g_0$", "MATH_0007": "$\\bar h = h_0$", "MATH_0008": "$f \\in \\mathbf{Z}_p[T]$", "MATH_0009": "$a_0 \\in \\mathbf{F}_p$", "MATH_0010": "$\\bar f(a_0) =0$", "MATH_0011": "$\\bar f'(a_0) \\neq 0$", "MATH_0012": "$a \\in \\mathbf{Z}_p$", "MATH_0013": "$f(a) = 0$", "MATH_0014": "$\\bar a = a_0$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f3aacdaabf46e7492e33679570cee659ad81b70a4bb74b05a33b49b001b37fc8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8f19c357f621e6d7fb4ac089303c2f2f6204d0f740d2016315f565392569d439", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall Hensel's lemma.\nThere are many versions of this lemma. Here are two:\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<ITEMOPEN_0001>(f)<ITEMCLOSE_0001> if <MATH_0001> monic and\n<MATH_0002> with <MATH_0003> then <MATH_0004> factors\nas <MATH_0005> with <MATH_0006> and <MATH_0007>,\n<ITEMOPEN_0002>(r)<ITEMCLOSE_0002> if <MATH_0008>, monic <MATH_0009>,\n<MATH_0010> but <MATH_0011>\nthen there exists <MATH_0012> with\n<MATH_0013> and <MATH_0014>.\n<STRUCT_0003>\nBoth versions are true (we will see this later). The first version\nasks for lifts of factorizations into coprime parts,\nand the second version asks for lifts of simple roots\nmodulo the maximal ideal. It turns out that requiring\nthese conditions for a general local ring are equivalent, and are\nequivalent to many other conditions. We use the root lifting\nproperty as the definition of a henselian local ring as it is\noften the easiest one to check.\n\n<COMMENT_0001>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dad28701df9489be46f228f19dc249c7f13f809618f0ea8dc181f457ccb4f48d", "unit_id": "tag:03QD:prose-0002"}
